  "note": "THE HARDEST OF THE THREE, because Seattle's character IS its topography and this framework flattens a city onto one tangent plane. Measured: downtown 35 m, Capitol Hill 107 m, Queen Anne 63 m, Elliott Bay -73 m. The inner radius is kept small (9 km) so the flattening covers the dense core and the hills beyond it survive. Also the first city with FRESH WATER: Lake Union reads +32 m in the coarse data, i.e. as land, so the water bake matters as much as the coastline.",
